WEBVTT

1
00:47:53.290 --> 00:47:56.290
We bless the name of Jesus this morning.

2
00:48:04.290 --> 00:48:11.290
Just tell Him this morning. King Jesus, we bless You this morning. All honor is for You.

3
00:48:11.290 --> 00:48:22.290
Yes. Hallelujah.

4
00:48:27.290 --> 00:48:33.290
You know, church, when you give Jesus the honor that He deserves, then your focus is on Him.

5
00:48:33.290 --> 00:48:41.290
During the prayer this morning, I prayed for this, that our focus is on Jesus.

6
00:48:41.290 --> 00:48:49.290
So when you sing, worthy is the lamb, and you focus yourself on what Jesus has done for us,

7
00:48:49.290 --> 00:48:53.290
then the focus is automatically no longer on your own.

8
00:48:53.290 --> 00:49:01.290
And that can be your own success, it can also be your struggles, the challenges in your life.

9
00:49:01.290 --> 00:49:07.290
That can be your family, that can be your financial situation, it can be anything.

10
00:49:07.290 --> 00:49:15.290
But Jesus says, if you look to me, then all other things will fall into place.

11
00:49:15.290 --> 00:49:23.290
Seek first God's kingdom and the rest is of secondary importance. It is important.

12
00:49:23.290 --> 00:49:28.290
It is important, and you have heard this all month long and today we will conclude with this,

13
00:49:28.290 --> 00:49:35.290
it is important to take good care of your relationships. It is important to take good care of your finances.

14
00:49:35.290 --> 00:49:44.290
It is important to place yourself in obedience and it is all important to do various things in a good way.

15
00:49:44.290 --> 00:49:52.290
But if you do all those things out of primary importance, then you ultimately forget to look to Jesus,

16
00:49:52.290 --> 00:50:00.290
while you must see everything through the lens of Jesus. So the focus must be, worthy is the lens.

17
00:50:00.290 --> 00:50:09.290
The focus must be, Jesus, I do everything through You and in You and with You and I do not want to do it without You.

18
00:50:09.290 --> 00:50:16.290
Lord, I do not want to go to my work without You. Lord, I do not want to be married to my life partner without You.

19
00:50:16.290 --> 00:50:23.290
Lord, I do not want to raise my children without You. Lord, I do not want to do my administration at all without You.

20
00:50:23.290 --> 00:50:34.290
I want to do it all with You. And that is why we sing, worthy is the lens. Hallelujah. Amen. Amen.

21
00:50:35.290 --> 00:50:41.290
We move on to the Word. We continue. Thank you, band.

22
00:50:41.290 --> 00:50:52.290
I want to take a moment to thank everyone super for what we have been able to do in the past time.

23
00:50:52.290 --> 00:50:57.290
We have started a project. I want to talk a little about the collections now.

24
00:50:58.290 --> 00:51:05.290
Some time ago, we started the Open Area project. I think you may have heard of it.

25
00:51:05.290 --> 00:51:14.290
I have also emailed about it. I have shown some things about it, and I hope you received the email last week.

26
00:51:14.290 --> 00:51:21.290
Because in that email last week, we were able to show that Open Area has started.

27
00:51:22.290 --> 00:51:29.290
People have become enthusiastic about it. People have given money to it. People have started to pray for it.

28
00:51:29.290 --> 00:51:36.290
People have the same vision through the Holy Spirit for what Open Church wants to do in our own area.

29
00:51:36.290 --> 00:51:41.290
Namely, we want to provide support to those who need it.

30
00:51:42.290 --> 00:51:54.290
And in the past few months, we have been working, embedded, and we have been thinking about what we can do to support this area.

31
00:51:54.290 --> 00:51:59.290
I had a conversation with the mayor, and I said to the mayor of Lommel.

32
00:51:59.290 --> 00:52:07.290
Mayor Nijs, what can we do to support this area? Where is there a real need?

33
00:52:08.290 --> 00:52:22.290
We were thinking about it. The mayor said, Tim, in this corona situation, in this time when schools sometimes have to close due to a risk of infection, children are sitting at home.

34
00:52:22.290 --> 00:52:27.290
And then they actually need to continue their lessons online at home.

35
00:52:28.290 --> 00:52:34.290
And you know, despite living in such a wealthy area, despite seeing wealth all around us.

36
00:52:34.290 --> 00:52:39.290
People are building careers, people can buy a house and a car, people are doing well.

37
00:52:39.290 --> 00:52:46.290
In general, we live in an area where people are financially okay.

38
00:52:46.290 --> 00:52:54.290
And so you would think that a developing country, somewhere on the other side of the world, that people there are poor.

39
00:52:54.290 --> 00:53:02.290
And then you might think to yourself, oh yes, I haven't seen any homeless people in Lommel, so there must be no poverty in Lommel.

40
00:53:02.290 --> 00:53:08.290
And yet, and yet unfortunately, there are people who are financially struggling.

41
00:53:08.290 --> 00:53:18.290
And yet, unfortunately, there are families who cannot simply buy a laptop so that their children can continue their lessons online.

42
00:53:19.290 --> 00:53:28.290
The mayor and I have discussed this, about the problem that these children end up staying at home and therefore cannot follow online lessons.

43
00:53:28.290 --> 00:53:38.290
And in the family, there is already a struggle with how the family cannot cope or cannot find a way to make ends meet financially.

44
00:53:38.290 --> 00:53:45.290
And then the child also faces a learning deficit, and the consequences can be far-reaching.

45
00:53:45.290 --> 00:53:55.290
And this is immediately, this is the wonderful project for Open Area. In this, we can participate, in this, we can support.

46
00:53:55.290 --> 00:54:06.290
And I started looking for a company that could help us. And what you have already seen in the email, if you have not received the email, make sure to sign up.

47
00:54:07.290 --> 00:54:15.290
Through the website openkerk.com you will see a registration form. Then you will receive every time we send an email, you will also get that email in your inbox.

48
00:54:15.290 --> 00:54:25.290
But I already wrote that it is simply miraculous that we as a church have been able to free up a budget of 13,000 euros.

49
00:54:25.290 --> 00:54:32.290
And that from that 13,000 euros we have been able to buy 58 so-called Chromebooks.

50
00:54:32.290 --> 00:54:42.290
These are laptops that can only be used online. But that is actually very nice, because there is no storage on the laptop, but the storage is in the cloud.

51
00:54:42.290 --> 00:54:52.290
Everything goes through the internet. And this is just right for students who need to follow online lessons. These are ideal laptops for these kinds of students.

52
00:54:53.290 --> 00:55:02.290
We have been able to buy 58 laptops. We have been able to give them to Lommel. And this has been the first project of Open Area.

53
00:55:02.290 --> 00:55:14.290
I want to say thank you. Thank you Open Church. Thank you Lord for giving us this initiative, for setting us to work, that we may do this for this area.

54
00:55:15.290 --> 00:55:22.290
Because I believe that we as a church are placed in an area to also have an impact in that area.

55
00:55:23.290 --> 00:55:31.290
Hallelujah. Super cool. And we will continue with Open Church. We will continue with Open Area.

56
00:55:31.290 --> 00:55:39.290
And I want to announce now, first of all for this week I want to say thank you for the donations that you give every week again.

57
00:55:39.290 --> 00:55:48.290
I want to thank you for the fact that despite this situation, despite this time when we cannot come together, I still see a lot of faithfulness on your part.

58
00:55:48.290 --> 00:55:55.290
That there is still giving to the church, so that we can still pay the bills and that we can just continue.

59
00:55:55.290 --> 00:56:03.290
Moreover, in the past few weeks, we have been working with all the leaders to write plans for the coming year.

60
00:56:03.290 --> 00:56:09.290
And do you know what is so important? There is still a good vision for the coming year.

61
00:56:09.290 --> 00:56:13.290
There is still a goal for the coming year to be able to build on.

62
00:56:13.290 --> 00:56:19.290
There is still for the coming year that we can say, guys, let's put our shoulders to the wheel.

63
00:56:19.290 --> 00:56:24.290
2021 will be a blessed year, just like 2020.

64
00:56:24.290 --> 00:56:29.290
Thank you for your gifts. Keep it up. Don't give up.

65
00:56:30.290 --> 00:56:39.290
Keep it up and realize that every euro you sow in the kingdom of God can help bring someone else to repentance.

66
00:56:39.290 --> 00:56:41.290
For that is why we live.

67
00:56:43.290 --> 00:56:53.290
Regarding open area, next week, December 6, we will hold a special collection for open area.

68
00:56:53.290 --> 00:56:55.290
For the Open Area project.

69
00:56:55.290 --> 00:57:02.290
Next week, December 6, we will hold a special collection solely for open area.

70
00:57:02.290 --> 00:57:05.290
And I can already tell you where this is going.

71
00:57:05.290 --> 00:57:13.290
Because after the Groonbroeks project, we have come up with a new project for which we have prayed.

72
00:57:13.290 --> 00:57:17.290
And what we are really excited about, and we are already super enthusiastic about it.

73
00:57:17.290 --> 00:57:25.290
And that is, we have made an agreement with Luikschestel, the plus in Luikschestel, from Huigevoort,

74
00:57:25.290 --> 00:57:32.290
that we can buy a number of Christmas packages from them.

75
00:57:32.290 --> 00:57:37.290
You know that in the past few years, we have done an action every time,

76
00:57:37.290 --> 00:57:42.290
that everyone from Open Church could bring all kinds of delicious products.

77
00:57:42.290 --> 00:57:47.290
While you come to church, you take something with you, a pack of spaghetti, a box of chocolates,

78
00:57:47.290 --> 00:57:50.290
toilet paper, everyone needs toilet paper this year.

79
00:57:50.290 --> 00:57:54.290
And so various people bring all sorts of things to church.

80
00:57:54.290 --> 00:58:00.290
And we would then put them in boxes and deliver them to the families who needed them.

81
00:58:00.290 --> 00:58:03.290
But this year we are not coming together as a church.

82
00:58:03.290 --> 00:58:07.290
And it would also be difficult to tell all the people of Open Church,

83
00:58:07.290 --> 00:58:13.290
just bring your things and bring your bottles of soda and boxes of chocolates,

84
00:58:13.290 --> 00:58:20.290
and cans of tuna and delicious liver pâté and all those things you can pack into a great package.

85
00:58:20.290 --> 00:58:26.290
This year it’s just not the case that we have that service and can organize that collection.

86
00:58:26.290 --> 00:58:32.290
And so we thought, wait a minute, the PLUS in Luikschestel,

87
00:58:33.290 --> 00:58:36.290
they sell those packages every year.

88
00:58:36.290 --> 00:58:40.290
You can save up for them or you can buy them for a certain amount.

89
00:58:40.290 --> 00:58:46.290
And they are boxes filled with all sorts of nice things.

90
00:58:46.290 --> 00:58:48.290
Those are the ideal Christmas packages.

91
00:58:48.290 --> 00:58:53.290
And it says in big letters worth 50 euros.

92
00:58:53.290 --> 00:58:57.290
And when you look in those boxes, there really is all sorts of delicious stuff in there.

93
00:58:57.290 --> 00:59:01.290
We are going to buy these boxes from PLUS Luikschestel.

94
00:59:01.290 --> 00:59:04.290
We have approached them, we have spoken with them.

95
00:59:04.290 --> 00:59:09.290
Debbie spoke with the director of PLUS Luikschestel, Mr. Van der Huijgenvoort, to say.

96
00:59:09.290 --> 00:59:12.290
We are Open Church, this is what we want to do.

97
00:59:12.290 --> 00:59:15.290
And how many packages can we buy from you?

98
00:59:15.290 --> 00:59:18.290
And what is a good deal we can make?

99
00:59:18.290 --> 00:59:22.290
Of course, we are not going to pay 50 euros for them, because they are worth 50 euros.

100
00:59:22.290 --> 00:59:29.290
But we want to get a good deal out of it, so that we can reach as many people as possible with such a package.

101
00:59:29.290 --> 00:59:32.290
PLUS Luikschestel was super enthusiastic about it.

102
00:59:32.290 --> 00:59:34.290
We are enthusiastic about it.

103
00:59:34.290 --> 00:59:37.290
Next week we are going to do a collector for this.

104
00:59:37.290 --> 00:59:41.290
So gather all the money you have together.

105
00:59:41.290 --> 00:59:45.290
And make sure we can collect it next week.

106
00:59:45.290 --> 00:59:49.290
So that we can do this second project from Open Area again.

107
00:59:49.290 --> 00:59:52.290
In Jesus' name. Amen. Amen.

108
00:59:52.290 --> 00:59:57.290
Bent, can I get an amen on that? Amen. Awesome.

109
00:59:59.290 --> 01:00:02.290
Thank you, Lord. Hallelujah. Thank you, Lord.

110
01:00:02.290 --> 01:00:06.290
Bent, thank you. Amen. Wonderful.

111
01:00:06.290 --> 01:00:08.290
Great is the Lord.

112
01:00:08.290 --> 01:00:11.290
Good morning, church. Good morning, church.

113
01:00:11.290 --> 01:00:14.290
Good morning, everyone. Yes.

114
01:00:14.290 --> 01:00:18.290
Shared to be in the kingdom of the Lord. Amen.

115
01:00:18.290 --> 01:00:21.290
We are blessed to sow in the kingdom of the Lord.

116
01:00:21.290 --> 01:00:24.290
And He is great. And He is true. Yes.

117
01:00:25.290 --> 01:00:29.290
He is truly worthy. Worthy of offerings. Worthy of gifts. Amen.

118
01:00:29.290 --> 01:00:31.290
He is worthy of our gifts.

119
01:00:31.290 --> 01:00:34.290
So we are going to the Word.

120
01:00:34.290 --> 01:00:38.290
This is the last week of Open Over Relationships.

121
01:00:38.290 --> 01:00:41.290
We are going to dive into the Word.

122
01:00:41.290 --> 01:00:44.290
This is the last week of Open About Relationships.

123
01:00:44.290 --> 01:00:49.290
And we are going to talk about raising godly children. Amen.

124
01:00:49.290 --> 01:00:54.290
And we are going to talk about raising children in God.

125
01:01:05.290 --> 01:01:08.290
So it is about upbringing, about parenthood.

126
01:01:08.290 --> 01:01:12.290
And we will cite some verses that form keys in this.

127
01:01:20.290 --> 01:01:26.290
You shall not follow the majority in evil.

128
01:01:26.290 --> 01:01:30.290
And it is forbidden to say You, for it is You.

129
01:01:30.290 --> 01:01:33.290
In Jesus' name. It is in the law of Moses.

130
01:01:33.290 --> 01:01:37.290
You shall not follow the majority in evil. Important.

131
01:01:50.290 --> 01:01:53.290
And I want to add another verse to that.

132
01:01:53.290 --> 01:01:59.290
The whole idea is based around the fact that we as children of God do not follow the culture,

133
01:01:59.290 --> 01:02:01.290
but that we take a different path.

134
01:02:13.290 --> 01:02:15.290
And this verse is so applicable.

135
01:02:15.290 --> 01:02:20.290
It is about Jeremiah 6, verse 16. And if you have a Bible, feel free to look it up.

136
01:02:35.290 --> 01:02:38.290
This takes place in the time when Jerusalem was besieged

137
01:02:38.290 --> 01:02:42.290
and when God had called the prophet Jeremiah to call the people back.

138
01:02:43.290 --> 01:02:46.290
To call them back to those ancient paths.

139
01:02:57.290 --> 01:03:01.290
And it is a warning. And it says, thus says the Lord.

140
01:03:01.290 --> 01:03:05.290
Stand at the crossroads. Think. Look to the ancient paths.

141
01:03:08.290 --> 01:03:11.290
And ask, which way leads to the good?

142
01:03:13.290 --> 01:03:15.290
And walk in it then.

143
01:03:17.290 --> 01:03:19.290
Take that path and find rest.

144
01:03:22.290 --> 01:03:24.290
But they say, we will not do that.

145
01:03:33.290 --> 01:03:38.290
I appoint watchmen or prophets over you. Pay attention to the sound of their ram's horn.

146
01:03:38.290 --> 01:03:40.290
But they say, we will not do that.

147
01:03:45.290 --> 01:03:47.290
Therefore, nations, listen.

148
01:03:51.290 --> 01:03:53.290
Come together and realize what is happening there.

149
01:03:55.290 --> 01:03:56.290
Earth, listen.

150
01:04:02.290 --> 01:04:05.290
I bring calamity upon that people and that is the fruit of their thoughts.

151
01:04:09.290 --> 01:04:15.290
Because they have not listened to my words and have rejected my laws.

152
01:04:25.290 --> 01:04:31.290
And we are the people of God and we live in a culture that has forsaken God.

153
01:04:39.290 --> 01:04:44.290
And as society departs and God’s words and the laws of God are disregarded,

154
01:04:44.290 --> 01:04:51.290
the more weariness you see in households, in relationships, in families.

155
01:05:08.290 --> 01:05:13.290
And actually, Jeremiah speaks about remaining on weary and tired paths.

156
01:05:13.290 --> 01:05:15.290
Stay on the old ways.

157
01:05:15.290 --> 01:05:20.290
Stay on the things of which God says, this is what causes the blessing.

158
01:05:31.290 --> 01:05:34.290
But what does a godless people or culture do?

159
01:05:34.290 --> 01:05:37.290
They say, we have no interest in God, we have no interest in His words.

160
01:05:37.290 --> 01:05:38.290
That is old.

161
01:05:38.290 --> 01:05:42.290
They even say that it is a way to tire it out, because it is old.

162
01:05:42.290 --> 01:05:45.290
This book is old, it is not relevant.

163
01:05:45.290 --> 01:05:49.290
But God says, it is older and it has been tested and is true.

164
01:05:49.290 --> 01:05:55.290
But a godless culture will say, that is an old book, it is an old way of life,

165
01:05:55.290 --> 01:05:57.290
we no longer need that.

166
01:05:57.290 --> 01:06:02.290
While God precisely says, my ways are tested and they are true.

167
01:06:08.290 --> 01:06:15.290
They are true and they bring not only truth and blessing to an individual household,

168
01:06:15.290 --> 01:06:17.290
but they do that for an entire country.

169
01:06:19.290 --> 01:06:25.290
I think that is important, because God's people are asked to live so differently,

170
01:06:25.290 --> 01:06:37.290
so blessed, so at rest in their souls, in the midst of chaos and things falling apart,

171
01:06:37.290 --> 01:06:40.290
because people have forsaken the old way of God.

172
01:06:50.290 --> 01:06:55.290
To live as God's people precisely in that rest that He gives.

173
01:06:55.290 --> 01:06:59.290
Amen, so we must not change the old boundaries,

174
01:06:59.290 --> 01:07:02.290
we must not change the markers,

175
01:07:02.290 --> 01:07:06.290
when people give other markers for relating,

176
01:07:06.290 --> 01:07:10.290
or other markers for, okay, God said it was this, but now we say it is this.

177
01:07:10.290 --> 01:07:16.290
That changes the boundaries, that changes the old way.

178
01:07:16.290 --> 01:07:18.290
That is what He means.

179
01:07:18.290 --> 01:07:23.290
Yes, the Bible does say this, but today we know that.

180
01:07:23.290 --> 01:07:24.290
We know something better.

181
01:07:24.290 --> 01:07:29.290
Yes, no, yes, but they said that back then, because that was their worldview at the time.

182
01:07:29.290 --> 01:07:31.290
As if families were different back then.

183
01:07:31.290 --> 01:07:33.290
As if people thought differently back then.

184
01:07:33.290 --> 01:07:39.290
Yes, so in other words, we must cling to the spoken and the truth,

185
01:07:39.290 --> 01:07:41.290
we must cling to God's Word and God's law.

186
01:07:41.290 --> 01:07:43.290
Exactly, yes.

187
01:07:43.290 --> 01:07:49.290
So let us follow those old ways of God, let us hold on to them.

188
01:07:50.290 --> 01:07:58.290
I want to, when you look at this and you read the Bible, you read God's Word,

189
01:07:58.290 --> 01:08:02.290
then you might read something that is a promise in God's Word,

190
01:08:02.290 --> 01:08:08.290
and maybe you think to yourself, yes, but I see what is written there,

191
01:08:08.290 --> 01:08:11.290
not manifesting in my own life,

192
01:08:11.290 --> 01:08:16.290
and then you might start to think, oh, maybe I need to approach it differently,

193
01:08:16.290 --> 01:08:21.290
or this isn't working so well, so I'll try something else instead,

194
01:08:21.290 --> 01:08:24.290
or I'll try some extra things.

195
01:08:24.290 --> 01:08:26.290
Let me give you an example.

196
01:08:26.290 --> 01:08:32.290
This is a Bible verse that I often refer to when it comes to raising children.

197
01:08:32.290 --> 01:08:39.290
These are key Bible verses that you should just write down somewhere,

198
01:08:39.290 --> 01:08:41.290
and you should read them regularly again.

199
01:08:41.290 --> 01:08:46.290
These are the pillars that stand from God's Word.

200
01:08:46.290 --> 01:08:48.290
It is Proverbs 22, verse 6.

201
01:08:48.290 --> 01:08:49.290
Here it comes.

202
01:08:49.290 --> 01:08:53.290
Teach your children how to live from a young age.

203
01:08:53.290 --> 01:08:55.290
Simple.

204
01:08:55.290 --> 01:08:56.290
It's not difficult.

205
01:08:56.290 --> 01:08:59.290
The Bible is not rocket science.

206
01:08:59.290 --> 01:09:01.290
It's rock science.

207
01:09:01.290 --> 01:09:02.290
It's solid.

208
01:09:02.290 --> 01:09:04.290
It's a given.

209
01:09:04.290 --> 01:09:06.290
The Bible is not difficult.

210
01:09:06.290 --> 01:09:08.290
It's instructive.

211
01:09:08.290 --> 01:09:11.290
It gives us goals for our lives.

212
01:09:11.290 --> 01:09:13.290
It provides us with instructions.

213
01:09:13.290 --> 01:09:19.290
And if you adhere to God's Word, you will also see the results of God's Word.

214
01:09:19.290 --> 01:09:21.290
But we will come back to this.

215
01:09:21.290 --> 01:09:23.290
So Proverbs 22, verse 6.

216
01:09:23.290 --> 01:09:27.290
Teach your children how to live from a young age.

217
01:09:27.290 --> 01:09:34.290
When they have grown up, they will continue on the same path.

