01:56:00.290 --> 01:56:16.290
And we said to each other, we are going to do that too.

956
01:56:16.290 --> 01:56:25.290
And when we were talking about it with them, he told us that he had been doing that for years and years and that it had just become a pattern.

957
01:56:25.290 --> 01:56:27.290
The rhythm was there.

958
01:56:46.290 --> 01:56:55.290
This also has to do with, oh sorry, first touch.

959
01:56:55.290 --> 01:57:01.290
And I really want to encourage young couples, look and ask for advice.

960
01:57:01.290 --> 01:57:10.290
When we were newly married, for example, within the first six months, I think we sat down with a counselor to simply ask for input.

961
01:57:10.290 --> 01:57:14.290
And then you still make your own choices, but ask for that advice.

962
01:57:15.290 --> 01:57:17.290
This also relates to Psalm 1.

963
01:57:17.290 --> 01:57:27.290
That you are blessed if you do not sit in the circle of mockers, but if you surround yourself with wise people.

964
01:57:27.290 --> 01:57:31.290
And so, you know what is so cool?

965
01:57:31.290 --> 01:57:39.290
When you are young, you can look around you and then you can, for example, take a generation that is just a bit further along than you.

966
01:57:39.290 --> 01:57:44.290
They have the experience and the Bible says, you can recognize a tree by its fruits.

967
01:57:44.290 --> 01:57:52.290
So it is very easy to choose someone you think, just look, they have already passed the test of time.

968
01:57:52.290 --> 01:57:56.290
They have already done this, I see that they walk with God, they still trust in God.

969
01:57:56.290 --> 01:57:58.290
And let those people go.

970
01:58:09.290 --> 01:58:35.290
We are going to close, shall we stand one more time and then we will just close.

971
